<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Absa half yr shr, div beat forecasts.</title>
<headline>Absa half yr shr, div beat forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr ended September 30</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	101.0	   vs 73.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    27.0	    vs 21.5</p>
<p>    Net income		   595	     vs 515</p>
<p>    Net interest income	2,654	   vs 2,159</p>
<p>    Other operating income   1,687	   vs 1,217</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 414	     vs 260</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			961	     vs 762</p>
<p>    Tax			    369	     vs 267</p>
<p>Div payable January 22</p>
<p>On register December 13</p>
<p>Full name: Amalgamated Banks of South Africa Ltd (banks and other financial services)</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast headline earnings rising to between 91.4 and 96.5 cents, with a consensus 94.6 cents. They expected the dividend to range between 25.5 cents and 28.3.</p>
<p>The bank said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
